{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_011: multimodal singleprofile scvi_n200+resnet50 concat, acc=53.6%, 0.56 GPU-hrs), the most critical uncertainty is which modality carries the primary signal. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a cheap unimodal baseline (~0.3-0.4 GPU-hrs, less than config_011 since no RNA encoding) that directly quantifies the image modality's standalone contribution. If image-only accuracy is close to 53.6%, RNA adds little and I should focus budget on image encoder upgrades (ViT-L) and multiprofile image aggregation. If it is substantially lower, the multimodal combination is genuinely valuable and I should invest in better RNA encoders and multiprofile aggregation. Resolving this modality-attribution question with a single cheap experiment is the highest-information-density next step before committing remaining budget to more expensive multiprofile/ViT-L configurations."
}

